# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages, mirroring nginx.conf (still used
# for local Docker preview only — see docker-compose.yml). connect-src
# includes https://api.request.tokyo because the API is now a separate
# origin (see src/api.ts / .env.production) rather than same-origin /api.
# connect-src also lists https://analytics.google.com and
# https://www.google.com (bare domains, not just the *.google-analytics.com/
# *.analytics.google.com wildcards) because gtag.js actually sends its
# collect hits to those exact hosts — a wildcard like *.analytics.google.com
# does NOT match the bare analytics.google.com, so without these gtag.js/
# boot.js loaded fine but every hit was silently dropped by the CSP.
# img-src includes https://api.request.tokyo for the same cross-origin-API
# reason as connect-src above — the 意思表示 broadcast image is served
# from GET /api/broadcast/image, and without this the <img> tag showing it
# is silently blocked the same way gtag's hits were.
# script-src also allows adm.shinobi.jp/cnobi.jp for the PC-only admax
# sticky-right ad loaded from boot.js, plus the fixed infra domains its SDK
# calls out to before it ever picks a creative: dmp.im-apps.net (user-id
# sync SDK), sync.shinobi.jp (cookie sync), and one inline bootstrap script
# admitted by hash (sha256-wAJZvpYF7i/hQGqXEF66seLFmPkYlUnRF1/om9+msWg=)
# rather than 'unsafe-inline'. img-src similarly allows adm.shinobi.jp
# itself (its /ib impression beacon) and the cookie-sync pixels of the ad
# exchanges admax's RTB auction calls out to: bidswitch.net, ad-stir.com,
# dsp.bance.jp, fout.jp. These were all found by opening request.tokyo with
# devtools open and reading the actual CSP violation errors — the SDK's
# bootstrap couldn't finish without them, so ads weren't just showing a
# blank creative, the auction pipeline itself never completed. Deliberately
# NOT widening img-src/frame-src further for the winning ad's own creative
# domain, since that rotates per-advertiser and isn't a fixed, enumerable
# set like the domains above; see boot.js.
# Also admax infra, found in a second devtools pass after the fix above:
# pb.shinobi.jp (script-src) is admax's passback loader — when the RTB
# auction has no winner, the /b/ response's tag_text loads
# pb.shinobi.jp/st/r.js + /t/<id> into the ad's about:blank iframe, which
# inherits this page's CSP, so it was blocked there. audiencedata.im-apps.net
# (connect-src) is the endpoint dmp.im-apps.net's im-uid.js SDK fetches the
# user id from. The passback waterfall pb.shinobi.jp returns (Criteo /
# PubMatic / AdStir scripts plus inline <script> blocks) is the rotating
# creative side and is intentionally NOT listed here either.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.googletagmanager.com https://adm.shinobi.jp https://cnobi.jp https://dmp.im-apps.net https://sync.shinobi.jp https://pb.shinobi.jp 'sha256-wAJZvpYF7i/hQGqXEF66seLFmPkYlUnRF1/om9+msWg='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://i.ytimg.com https://*.ytimg.com https://*.nimg.jp https://*.vimeocdn.com https://api.request.tokyo https://adm.shinobi.jp https://x.bidswitch.net https://bypass.ad-stir.com https://tr.dsp.bance.jp https://sync.fout.jp; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://embed.nicovideo.jp https://player.vimeo.com; connect-src 'self' https://audiencedata.im-apps.net https://api.request.tokyo https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://www.google.com https://www.googletagmanager.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
